  "published": "2026-08-12T08:57:06.827Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.6.2\n      - Added PdfRequest.SkipTrailingBlankPage + PdfRequestBuilder.WithSkipTrailingBlankPage(): suppresses the trailing blank page produced when the document's last element carries page-break-after: always / break-after: page. Honoured by CobaltPDF (Chromium) 1.6.3+ and CobaltPDF.WebKit 1.6.4+; older servers ignore the property, so mixed-version client/server combinations keep working.\n\n      v1.6.1\n      - Added PdfRequest.Compress (default true) + PdfRequestBuilder.WithCompression(bool): controls output PDF compression (maps to the editions' WithCompression(bool)). Legacy SkipPostProcessing / WithSkipPostProcessing() retained as the inverse for back-compat (builder deprecated).\n      - Added PdfRequest.ViewportWidth / ViewportHeight + PdfRequestBuilder.WithViewportSize(width[, height]): sets the render viewport; a tall height triggers IntersectionObserver lazy images without scrolling.\n      - Added PdfRequest.ForceEagerImages + PdfRequestBuilder.WithEagerImages(): forces lazy-loaded images (loading=\"lazy\" and data-src/data-srcset) to load before rendering.\n      - All additive and honoured by both the CobaltPDF (Chromium) and CobaltPDF.WebKit 1.6.0 editions. Object-initializer construction is unchanged.\n\n      v1.6.0\n      - Added a fluent builder for PdfRequest, mirroring the CobaltEngine fluent API: PdfRequest.ForUrl(url) / PdfRequest.ForHtml(html), chained .WithPaperFormat/.WithMargins/.WithHeader/.WithWatermark/.WithEncryption/.WithMetadata/.AddCookie/... then .Build(). PdfRequest.ToBuilder() adapts an existing instance. The fluent path produces an identical PdfRequest (and identical JSON) to the object-initializer style.",
